    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302-a3">

                <pb facs="0477" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg383"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    191—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Faine to Mr. Smythe.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1896-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                                1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Sec. No. 48.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I make it my duty to bring to your
                    attention that the department of the interior, in view of the conduct of Mr.
                    Hugo Loewi, American citizen, has been under the necessity to take the measure
                    of expulsion against your subject (ressortisant), whose residence in our
                    territory can no longer be tolerated without danger to the public order and
                    tranquillity.</p>
                <p>I transmit to you, herewith inclosed, a copy of the decree of expulsion.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Faine</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Relations.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
